{
 "schema": 1,
 "name": "diagrams-llm",
 "description": "LLM-written diagrams with their surrounding prose, labelled by hand per diagram rule. Measures recall and precision of the diagram pack; the human diagrams in corpus/diagrams only bound false positives.",
 "origin": "authored-llm",
 "license": "Apache-2.0",
 "provenance": {
  "author": {
   "agent": "opencode coder subagent for bead slopvac-8l4.10.9",
   "model": "Claude Sonnet 5.5 (Global)",
   "provider": "amazon-bedrock",
   "model_id": "global.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5"
  },
  "date": "2026-11-16",
  "method": "Written in context by the agent in one session. No model API was called to sample the diagrams, and no sample was drawn from a public source.",
  "instruction": "Write LLM-style diagrams (Mermaid and PlantUML fenced in Markdown with the paragraphs before and after, and draw.io files), as an assistant writes them in documentation and answers: positives that carry each target pattern of diagram.label-run-on, label-title-plus-gloss, note-long, meta-reference and prose-restates-labels, and clean negatives, including near misses and boundary cases (six words against seven, a five-word note against six). Include title-cased glosses after a line break and after a colon (PR 452 trade-off). Label each sample by hand from the rule definitions in crates/slopvac-diagrams/pack/diagram.json, not from rule output.",
  "limitations": [
   "The author read the rule definitions and thresholds, so the positives are close to the rule wording and recall is likely higher than on unprompted model output.",
   "One author and one annotator: labels carry no inter-annotator agreement.",
   "Samples are short and synthetic. draw.io files have no prose, so the prose rules have no draw.io positives.",
   "The set is small (see labels.json); every rate carries a wide Wilson interval."
  ]
 },
 "labels": "labels.json",
 "label_semantics": "Each label names a rule and a text that the rule's finding should contain. An empty text means one finding of the rule anywhere in the document. A sample with no labels is a clean negative.",
